Original commit body from bfc80a2a1bd407e4e8248ac6ed2588a4b47ef490:

INV-kagib: the OCaml, Agda, Lean and Wolfram analyzers kept a per-file
set of seen names, so the second same-name declaration of a file was
absent from the graph: `run` in a second OCaml/Agda module or Lean
namespace, a second Agda record's `field fst`, the Wolfram overload
`run[x_String]` beside `run[x_Integer]`. Every declaration is now
emitted with its scope chain:

- ocaml: each let binding (every `and` binding, shadowing
  redefinitions) is a symbol; module-nested bindings are named `A.run`
  (`A.C.deep`); local functions keep their bare name with `f/g` in the
  chain; local `let x = ... in` values are no longer emitted as
  functions. Types/modules are emitted per declaration under their bare
  names (table-formula ids, unchanged). Calls anchor by position and a
  `A.run` call tries the qualified name first.
- agda: chain over nested modules (`module _` adds nothing), data types,
  records and where-owners; `A.run`, `Pair.fst`, constructors bare with
  the data type in the chain; reference sources found by chain.
- lean: namespace stack over namespace/section/end (`_root_` opts out);
  `A.run`, `B.foo`; an unnamed instance keeps the class name with its
  type application in the chain; struct/class keep table ids. Reference
  sources found by position.
- wolfram: definitions read from the left-hand side text (the grammar
  does not parse blank patterns; `helper[] := 2` was missed); patterns
  become meta.parameters with heads/tests/literals as types (typed
  tier), `__`/`___`/OptionsPattern variadic, `x_:d`/`x_.` defaults.
- fsharp: nested-module chain (`A.run`, `A.Point.X`, class-level
  `Shape.helper`), local functions chained `outer/inner`; dotted calls
  try the qualified name first. Class types and members are still not
  emitted (filed WI-tamib).
- tlaplus: LET-local operators chained by their enclosing operators
  (`A/f`), higher-order parameters counted; reference sources by
  position and LET-locals resolved by scope before the repo lookup.
- haskell: arity from the first equation's patterns (meta.arity).
- elm: parameters from the function's patterns.

All mint the ADR-0035 producer formula through
overload_arity.declared_arity_stable_id; non-callable kinds that rode
the floor are migrated too (haskell data/instance, fsharp
record/union/field, elm port, agda data/record/field, lean
theorem/inductive/instance, tlaplus constant/theorem/assumption).

Floor/null -> producer only: every previously producer-computed id is
byte-identical on the gate fixtures and a corpus sample (40 files per
language where available). Baseline: the eight languages leave
floor_and_null and the six failing ones leave sibling_deletion_moves.
Producer-count docs for meta.parameters updated; stale lean/tlaplus
line citations in symbol_kinds.py / concept-axes.md repointed.

